It looks difficult, but one might notice that $H_{n+1} = H_n + 1/H_n$ and that
\[\frac{1}{n H_n H_{n+1}} = \frac{1}{n H_n (H_n + 1/H_n)} = \frac{1}{n H_n^2} - \frac{1}{n + 1 H_n^2}.\]We then get pretty much everything that we need.
</think>
\begin{align*}
\sum_{n = 1}^\infty \frac{1}{(n + 1) H_n H_{n + 1}} &= \sum_{n = 1}^\infty \left( \frac{1}{n H_n^2} - \frac{1}{(n + 1) H_{n + 1}^2}\right) \\ &= \lim_{N \to \infty} \left( \frac{1}{H_1} - \frac{1}{(N + 1) H_{N + 1}^2} \right) \\ &= 1 - 0 \\ &= 1.
\end{align*}
